  "narrative": {
    "schema": "scholar-portrait-0.1",
    "field": {
      "en": "Harmonic analysis, probability, combinatorics and the mathematical foundations of signal recovery, with a side habit of writing expository texts.",
      "zh": "调和分析、概率论、组合数学与信号恢复的数学基础，并兼有撰写教材式阐释的习惯。"
    },
    "theme": {
      "en": "Turning a hard problem into a convex, certificate-bearing one, then proving the reduction is sharp.",
      "zh": "把难题转化为带证书的凸问题，再证明这种转化已达最优。"
    },
    "lead": {
      "en": "These papers repeatedly take an apparently impossible inverse problem—recover a signal from too few, noisy, or corrupted measurements—and show that a simple convex program succeeds, then pin down the thresholds where it must. The same move recurs from sparse recovery and the Dantzig selector to nuclear-norm matrix completion, always with constants, probabilities, and near-optimality. A separate strand builds abstract machinery, such as Strichartz estimates or transference principles, as reusable tools for other problems. The habit is constructive reduction plus honest accounting of limits.",
      "zh": "这批论文反复处理一类看似不可能的逆问题——从过少、含噪或受损的测量中恢复信号——先证明一个简单的凸规划即可成功，再精确刻画它必然奏效的阈值。从稀疏恢复、Dantzig选择子到核范数矩阵补全，这一手法不断重现，并总伴随显式常数、概率界与近最优性。另一条线索则搭建抽象工具，如Strichartz估计或转移原理，供别的问题复用。其习惯是构造性的归约，并如实交代边界。"
    },
    "person": {
      "name": {
        "en": "Jean-Baptiste Joseph Fourier",
        "zh": "让-巴蒂斯特·约瑟夫·傅里叶"
      },
      "wikiTitle": "Joseph_Fourier",
      "connection": {
        "en": "Fourier's practice was to recast a physical problem in a new representation—trigonometric series—and then argue that the representation is general and that coefficients determine the object. These papers do the inverse: they ask how few Fourier or random linear measurements suffice, and prove exact or stable recovery with thresholds. The shared intellectual move is treating a transform as an analytic instrument whose completeness and limits can be quantified.",
        "zh": "傅里叶的做法是把物理问题换到一种新表示——三角级数——再论证这种表示具有普遍性、系数决定对象。这批论文走的是反方向：追问需要多少个傅里叶测量或随机线性测量才够，并给出精确或稳定恢复的阈值。共同的思想动作是把一种变换当作可被量化其完备性与极限的分析仪器。"
      },
      "paperIds": [
        "W2145096794",
        "W2129638195",
        "W2164452299"
      ],
      "boundary": {
        "en": "Fourier sought a universal representation for arbitrary functions; these papers instead exploit sparsity or low rank, so recovery depends on a structural prior that Fourier's program did not require.",
        "zh": "傅里叶追求对任意函数的普遍表示；这批论文则利用稀疏性或低秩，恢复依赖某种结构先验，这是傅里叶纲领所不需要的。"
      }
    },
    "traits": [
      {
        "title": {
          "en": "Convex relaxation with matching lower bounds",
          "zh": "凸松弛与配套下界"
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "The sparse-recovery and matrix-completion papers do not merely propose a tractable program; each pairs it with an information-theoretic benchmark. Sparse spikes are recovered from about |T| log N frequencies and no method can do much better; low-rank matrices are recovered near the sampling limit. This pairing of algorithm and impossibility is the signature.",
          "zh": "稀疏恢复与矩阵补全的论文不只是提出可计算的程序，而是各自配上信息论基准。稀疏尖峰从约 |T| log N 个频率中恢复，任何方法都难以更好；低秩矩阵的恢复也逼近采样极限。算法与不可能性成对出现，是最鲜明的标志。"
        },
        "paperIds": [
          "W2145096794",
          "W2134332047",
          "W2164452299"
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": {
          "en": "From exact to stable, noisy, adversarial",
          "zh": "从精确到稳定、含噪、对抗"
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "A first exact-recovery theorem is soon extended: noise gives error within the noise level, gross corruption is handled by ℓ1 decoding, and the Dantzig selector bounds estimation error against an oracle. The pattern is to stress-test the clean theorem until it resembles a real measurement channel, while keeping nonasymptotic constants.",
          "zh": "精确恢复定理很快被推广：噪声下误差不超过噪声水平，大量损坏由 ℓ1 译码处理，Dantzig选择子则给出相对理想情形的估计误差界。其模式是不断对干净定理施压，直到它接近真实测量通道，同时保留非渐近常数。"
        },
        "paperIds": [
          "W2164452299",
          "W2129131372",
          "W403935824"
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": {
          "en": "Abstract estimates as reusable instruments",
          "zh": "把抽象估计做成可复用仪器"
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "The endpoint Strichartz work proves an abstract estimate that yields several concrete cases at once, and the primes paper isolates a transference principle as the new engine. Likewise the multilinear restriction paper replaces a hard conjecture with a controlled multilinear analogue. The recurring style is to find the right general statement that makes many instances fall out.",
          "zh": "端点Strichartz工作证明一个抽象估计，一次给出多个具体情形；素数论文则把转移原理提炼为新引擎。多线性限制性论文同样用受控的多线性版本替代困难猜想。反复出现的风格是找到恰当的一般陈述，使许多实例自然落出。"
        },
        "paperIds": [
          "W2102327241",
          "W2097673562",
          "W2164774824"
        ]
      }
    ],
